 lar papers and July 7 for special sessions\, both 23:59 AoE. Recent 2024-
 2026 editions support an annual planning cadence. S is an editorial estim
 ate\; no ICORE or CCF rank is borrowed from related venues.\nScope: Visua
 l information processing across image\, video\, 3D\, and unconventional s
 ensing modalities. Its defining areas are computational imaging\, restora
 tion and enhancement\, coding\, recognition\, multimodal fusion\, and sub
 jective/objective quality assessment. Rendering and visualizing data\, hu
 man/biometric analysis\, and robust evaluation are recurring strands. An 
 extensive applications list is not treated as equal coverage of every app
 lication domain or every responsible-AI subtopic.\nAdditional topics: Mul
 timedia Learning & Retrieval\, Computer Graphics & Visualization\, Biomet
 rics & Human Sensing\, Robustness & Safety\nScope sources (2026): https:/
 /euvip2026.github.io/C4P.pdf\, https://euvip2026.github.io/calls/\nScope 
 last checked: 2026-10-07
URL:https://euvip2026.github.io/
END:VEVENT
